choice AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_TYPE
    prompt "Microphone hardware type"
    default AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_SPH0655_PDM
    help
        Select the microphone hardware connected to the audio capture peripheral.
        ES8311: Analog codec via I2C + I2S (legacy board).
        SPH0655: PDM digital microphone on the V2 N16R8 CLK/DOUT interface.

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_ES8311
    bool "ES8311 analog codec (legacy board)"

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_SPH0655_PDM
    bool "SPH0655 PDM digital mic (V2 N16R8)"

endchoice

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_V2_MIC_INTERFACE_VALIDATED
    bool "Enable V2 microphone capture after CLK/DOUT interface validation"
    default n
    depends on AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_SPH0655_PDM
    help
        Enable only for V2 hardware validation builds that must exercise the
        CLK/GPIO48 and DOUT/GPIO47 microphone path. When disabled, firmware
        reports a degraded audio path instead of pretending capture is ready.

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_PDM_AFE_WEBRTC
    bool "Use continuous WebRTC AFE for the V2 PDM microphone"
    default y
    depends on AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_SPH0655_PDM
    help
        Process the selected PDM microphone channel through ESP-SR's
        continuous WebRTC noise suppression and automatic gain control before
        BLE transmission. This has no voice-gated startup path: every captured
        frame is processed so the preview and final transcript receive the
        same audio stream.

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_PDM_STEREO_SLOT_CAPTURE
    bool "Read the SPH0655 PDM multiplexed slot"
    default y
    depends on AUDIO_CAPTURE_MIC_SPH0655_PDM
    help
        Listener V2.2 hardwires SPH0655 SELECT to VSS. Per the Knowles timing
        contract, that microphone drives the falling-edge PDM slot. The
        Listener V2.2 hardware capture validation maps that signal to the
        ESP32-S3 driver's left PCM slot with clk_inv disabled. Mono mode does
        not preserve an explicit channel selection, so keep this enabled.

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_SPH0655_SLOT_RIGHT
    bool "Use the right PDM slot for the SPH0655"
    default n
    depends on AUDIO_CAPTURE_PDM_STEREO_SLOT_CAPTURE
    help
        The SPH0655 SELECT strap is a board property, not a signal that may be
        inferred from boot-time ambient noise. Listener V2.2 ties SELECT to
        VSS and its physical capture validation selects the left PCM channel;
        leave this disabled for that board. Enable only for a board whose
        measured I2S mapping selects the right PCM channel.

config AUDIO_CAPTURE_SPH0655_CLK_INVERT
    bool "Invert the PDM clock for the SPH0655 timing strap"
    default n
    depends on AUDIO_CAPTURE_PDM_STEREO_SLOT_CAPTURE
    help
        Select the clock polarity validated against the SPH0655's SELECT strap.
        This is a board-timing property and is never inferred from ambient audio.
